## Big-O Time Complexity

| Method | Time Complexity | Explanation |
|---|---|---|
| `addSong()` | O(1) average | Adds a song to the end of the doubly linked list and inserts it into the HashMaps. |
| `findSong()` | O(1) average | Uses a HashMap to find a song by ID. |
| `showPlaylist()` | O(n) | Traverses the playlist to collect all song titles. |
| `play()` | O(1) average | Finds the song using a HashMap and updates the current song and history stack. |
| `nowPlaying()` | O(1) | Returns the current song directly. |
| `playCount()` | O(1) average | Looks up a song's play count in a HashMap. |
| `queueLater()` | O(1) average | Adds a song to the end of the deque. |
| `queueNext()` | O(1) average | Adds a song to the front of the deque. |
| `showUpNext()` | O(q) | Traverses the up-next deque to collect queued song titles. |
| `next()` | O(q) worst case | May skip multiple invalid entries in the up-next deque before finding a valid song. |
| `back()` | O(h) worst case | May pop multiple invalid entries from history before finding a valid song. |
| `showHistory()` | O(h) | Traverses the history stack to collect song titles. |
| `removeSong()` | O(1) average | Finds the node using a HashMap and removes it from the doubly linked list without searching. |

### Variables

- `n` = number of songs in the playlist.
- `q` = number of entries in the up-next deque.
- `h` = number of entries in the history stack.

**Note:** HashMap operations take O(1) time on average. The `next()` and `back()` methods may take longer when skipping entries for songs that have been removed.
